/**
 * Inline image fixtures for stories (issue #352).
 *
 * The page-fixture rules in src/pages/fixtures.ts keep story
 * screenshots deterministic — no network, no clocks — and these
 * constants extend the same rule to stories that must render an
 * actual image (Thumbnail's cover-crop shapes, Avatar's image
 * form, ImportReviewPage's hero banner). They used to point at
 * picsum.photos URLs: the image then loads over the network, so
 * a capture can catch it in either load state and the same head
 * produces different screenshots across passes (the
 * ImportReviewPage with-image verify flake in #352). A data URI
 * renders identically on every run, on web and native alike.
 *
 * The images are small generated placeholders — a warm gradient
 * "plated dish" — drawn once and committed as base64 JPEG; they
 * are fixture data, not artwork. Regenerate by re-rendering the
 * same drawing, never by fetching a remote photo.
 */

